1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,218
This is WQ-LS,

2
00:00:01,238 --> 00:00:05,169
an industrial direct-drive lockstitch machine designed from scratch with AI

3
00:00:05,189 --> 00:00:05,801
at WenQuest,

4
00:00:06,271 --> 00:00:10,006
from a design brief to a virtual prototype that sews on the web.

5
00:00:10,726 --> 00:00:13,444
The documentation opens on the virtual prototype:

6
00:00:13,614 --> 00:00:19,380
116 parts, every one a real design solid, sewing at 5000 stitches a minute.

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:24,416
How was it designed? People set the direction and make the choices: how fast,

8
00:00:24,436 --> 00:00:26,331
which look, whether to lighten it.

9
00:00:26,801 --> 00:00:29,335
AI writes the calculations, builds the 3-D solids, runs the simulations,

10
00:00:29,355 --> 00:00:30,541
produces drawings and NC programs,

11
00:00:30,711 --> 00:00:34,484
and checks itself with tests — change one thing and everything downstream is

12
00:00:34,504 --> 00:00:35,032
recomputed.

13
00:00:35,752 --> 00:00:38,111
And it all runs on WenQuest's own software:

14
00:00:38,131 --> 00:00:40,877
the sewing-machine design tool for the mechanisms,

15
00:00:41,347 --> 00:00:43,929
digital-factory CAE for FEA, casting and multibody dynamics,

16
00:00:44,099 --> 00:00:48,110
WenQuest NC programming for machining, WenQuest Electronics for the controller,

17
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:50,049
and web 3-D to put the machine online.

18
00:00:50,769 --> 00:00:55,112
The design runs through ten gates: brief, dynamics, styling and housing,

19
00:00:55,132 --> 00:00:57,415
parts and mechanisms, housing process,

20
00:00:57,885 --> 00:01:01,115
web 3-D, drawings and BOM, virtual-prototype validation,

21
00:01:01,135 --> 00:01:03,611
plus the controller and a company standard.

22
00:01:04,331 --> 00:01:07,593
Gate one fixes the scheme: what the needle, take-up,

23
00:01:07,613 --> 00:01:10,686
hook and feed mechanisms each do within one turn.

24
00:01:11,406 --> 00:01:13,901
The timing diagram drives the 3-D machine:

25
00:01:13,921 --> 00:01:18,451
the hook point passes behind the needle at 206 degrees and catches the loop,

26
00:01:18,621 --> 00:01:20,792
with exactly two millimetres of needle rise.

27
00:01:21,512 --> 00:01:25,868
Gate two is dynamics: the inertia of every moving part plus piercing,

28
00:01:25,888 --> 00:01:27,518
thread and feed resistance

29
00:01:27,688 --> 00:01:31,126
add up to the shaft torque — peaking under five newton-metres,

30
00:01:31,146 --> 00:01:32,799
averaging under seventy watts.

31
00:01:33,519 --> 00:01:35,576
How big is the balance weight?

32
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:40,215
Drag the ratio and the shaking force drops from 690 to 415 newtons;

33
00:01:40,235 --> 00:01:41,738
0.6 is the sweet spot.

34
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:44,648
The upper shaft is checked by finite elements:

35
00:01:44,668 --> 00:01:47,195
73 megapascals at the small fillet by the crank seat,

36
00:01:47,365 --> 00:01:50,120
a safety factor of nearly five against yield.

37
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:53,528
Gate three picks the look — streamlined option B —

38
00:01:53,698 --> 00:01:56,173
and the housing becomes two HT250 castings,

39
00:01:56,193 --> 00:01:59,712
with walls and ribs sized step by step to a stiffness target.

40
00:02:00,432 --> 00:02:02,558
Gate four turns every part into a solid;

41
00:02:02,578 --> 00:02:05,134
the take-up four-bar can be resized on the spot,

42
00:02:05,304 --> 00:02:08,929
and thread supply and demand for three fabrics are recomputed at once.

43
00:02:09,649 --> 00:02:11,702
Gate five is the housing process:

44
00:02:11,722 --> 00:02:16,224
a solidification simulation shows the iron freezing from the outside in,

45
00:02:16,943 --> 00:02:19,420
and the tools of eight NC programs follow their real paths.

46
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:23,644
Gates six and seven put the machine on the web and generate the BOMs and

47
00:02:23,664 --> 00:02:26,189
drawings of eight variants straight from the design;

48
00:02:26,359 --> 00:02:28,308
click a line and the part flies out.

49
00:02:29,028 --> 00:02:31,385
Gate eight validates the virtual prototype:

50
00:02:31,405 --> 00:02:34,204
nineteen assembly steps along real insertion paths,

51
00:02:34,924 --> 00:02:38,470
and 285 part pairs checked for clearance turn by turn.

52
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:42,305
Multibody dynamics re-solves the whole machine in MuJoCo,

53
00:02:42,325 --> 00:02:44,505
within 0.14 percent of the power method,

54
00:02:45,225 --> 00:02:48,685
with every joint force and every part's inertia force visible.

55
00:02:49,405 --> 00:02:52,695
The controller firmware really runs in a simulator:

56
00:02:52,715 --> 00:02:55,031
zero to 5000 in a tenth of a second,

57
00:02:55,201 --> 00:02:59,077
then trim, needle-up stop, wipe and foot lift, step by step.

58
00:02:59,797 --> 00:03:03,497
One person with AI and WenQuest's software, ten gates in days.

59
00:03:03,967 --> 00:03:06,181
Every number comes from AI's design calculations,

60
00:03:06,201 --> 00:03:09,645
and every figure can be opened, dragged and recomputed in the documentation.

61
00:03:09,815 --> 00:03:11,670
That is AI-native design at WenQuest.
